scription": "1. Check for consciousness: Approach the collapsed person and determine if they are conscious.\n2. Establish an airway: If the person is conscious, support their neck and tilt their chin back to establish an airway.\n3. What to do if unconscious: If the person is not breathing, call 911 and describe the situation.\n4. Prepare to use an AED: Locate and move to the nearest AED box.\n5. Apply the AED: Place the AED near the collapsed person and press the power button to activate the machine.\n6. Apply patches: Unbutton the person's shirt and place the AED patches over the right chest and next to the left chest.\n7. Shock: Press the defibrillation button to deliver an electric shock, keeping your distance from the victim.\n8. CPR: Continue CPR after defibrillation, using two hands at a rate of 100 compressions per minute.\n9. Check and repeat: Ends if the patient regains consciousness, but if they don't improve, check their condition and repeat the entire process if necessary.", "short_description": "Learn how to use an Automated External Defibrillator (AED). This life-saving skill is essential in emergency situations where someone is experiencing cardiac arrest."}]}, "developer_name": null, "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://training.contentsda.kr/privacy-policy-en/", "developer_terms_of_service_url": "https://training.contentsda.kr/terms-and-conditions-en/", "publisher_name": "ContentsDa Inc", "support_website_url": null, "website_url": "https://training.contentsda.kr/", "category": null, "comfort_rating": "NOT_RATED", "comfort_tags": [], "context_category": {"id": "362692211442873", "context_category": "APPS"}, "context_topics": [{"id": "1043107547362485"}, {"id": "514087707868786"}], "external_subscription_type": "NOT_REQUIRED", "genres": [], "has_in_app_ads": null, "internet_connection": "NOT_REQUIRED", "play_area": "MOVEMENT", "recommended_graphics": null, "recommended_memory_gb": null, "recommended_processor": null, "supported_in_app_languages"